spoiler follows


 Here's what I know so far about this one. This is just a tiny bit more
 than I knew last time I posted it.

 Basic method: Get a bag of holding. Fill it with as much junk as you
 can carry (I drop everything else nonessential to really load the 
 sucker up). Curse it. Remove the junk. Uncurse it.

 Result: the bag apparently has a negative weight. You can carry till you've
 used all your inventory letters plus more in the bag, but it's
 not infinite capacity. Also lets you squeeze into the openings on
 boulders and you'll also never get the "you are carrying too much 
 to get through" message -- both of these are apparently determined by weight.
 You can ultimately not be able to carry more. If you still *need* more,
 you have to do it again.

 Observations: the apparent negative weight (i.e. how much you can carry) seems
 to depend on how much stuff (i.e. the weight) of the bag before cursing.
 You can do this with an empty bag, but it doesn't wind up letting you 
 carry as much -- actually with an empty bag it seems to only let you carry
 a bit more (my experience). So the negative weight of the bag after this 
 seems to depend on its weight when cursed. If you're carrying a whole mess
 of stuff and drop the treated bag, you collapse under your weight. Pick the
 bag up again and you're cruising. You can iterate the procedure
 of filling/cursing/emptying (may be optional)/uncursing to make the
 weight more negative (and hence further increase your carrying capacity).

 Don't Know: if you have to remove all the stuff from the bag before 
 uncursing it. I do this; in fact I make all the stuff disappear (if you
 try to remove stuff from a cursed boh, it has a chance to disappear).
 Since I only put junk in, I don't care about this. I always want to
 empty the bag anyway.

 Cautions: never put a wand of cancellation of a bag of holding into a 
 bag of holding. Bag and contents explode. Never put an artifact into
 a bag of holding -- it can lose its named status.

 I think that if you put everything into the neg. weight boh then it does
 something funny to your ability to hit -- I haven't checked this.

 It's a cool trick --- you can be carrying *tons* of stuff and as long as
 you have a free inventory letter, still pick up a dragon corpse and 
 scoot over to that altar.....

 That's it.....
